From: OpenIPC
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt7601sta: stop indicating a link down while the link comes up

LinkUp() indicates a media disconnect before completing, meant for a roam from a
different SSID. It fires on a first association too, because LastSsid still holds a
previous value at that point, and wpa_supplicant reads it as the AP going away: it
drops to SCANNING with bssid 00:00:00:00:00:00 and defers every EAPOL frame of the
4-way handshake, so the port never secures and the AP deauthenticates with Reason=15.
A real disconnection is already indicated by the LinkDown path.

--- a/sta/connect.c
+++ b/sta/connect.c
@@ -2140,9 +2140,13 @@
 					break;
 				}
 			}
-			/* Send link down event before set to link up */
-			RTMP_IndicateMediaState(pAd, NdisMediaStateDisconnected);
-			pAd->ExtraInfo = GENERAL_LINK_DOWN;
+			/* No link down is indicated here. This runs while the link is
+			 * coming up, and wpa_supplicant reads it as the AP going away: it
+			 * drops to SCANNING with bssid 00:00:00:00:00:00 and then defers
+			 * every EAPOL frame of the 4-way handshake, so the port never
+			 * secures and the AP deauthenticates with Reason=15. A real
+			 * disconnection is already indicated by the LinkDown path.
+			 */
 			DBGPRINT(RT_DEBUG_TRACE, ("NDIS_STATUS_MEDIA_DISCONNECT Event AA!\n"));
 			break;
 		}
